diff --git a/PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md b/PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md
index 4f4c2fa6c2..cef3203ea9 100644
--- a/PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md
@@ -65,6 +65,8 @@
 
 ## Maintenance
 
+- **CI runners:** Switched GitHub Actions jobs from GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-latest` runners to the `namespace-profile-axios` Namespace runner profile. The npm publish job stays on `ubuntu-latest` because npm provenance and trusted publishing require GitHub-hosted runners. CI only; no runtime, public API, or type compatibility changes.
+
 - **Packaged end-to-end suites:** Replace the mocked compatibility/smoke projects with a top-level `tests/` e2e workspace. Build and pack the current Axios package, verify a checksum manifest, and install it into isolated consumers outside the repository. Exercise real local HTTP/HTTPS/HTTP2 services, proxies, faults, browser applications, CORS/cookies/XSRF, streams, uploads, progress, and cancellation using Playwright's three browser engines and native Node.js/Bun/Deno runners. Retain declaration coverage with compiled installed-package applications and keep every existing unit, source-browser, and artifact test unchanged. Add focused unit regression cases for exceptional cleanup in custom Fetch environments. Record the public issue/PR title/body screening and test inventory with coverage and expansion limits. Canonicalize temporary paths so symlinked temporary directories remain valid, isolate UMD and proxy assertions from earlier consumers, verify actual CONNECT tunnels, and terminate timed-out or interrupted command trees, including nested process groups, with real worker-cleanup regression checks. Allow bounded signal cleanup before forcing termination so interrupted packing cannot leave workers listening. CI and release preparation share the same package across every runtime lane, bootstrap pnpm from a checksum-verified tarball in the e2e jobs, and reference the reusable workflow with GitHub’s self-repository syntax; old module/smoke commands are replaced by `test:e2e` commands. No runtime dependency or package export changes. ([#11364](https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/11364))
 
 - **Repository OSS skills:** Check in the five maintainer-installed `oss-*` workflows under `.agents/skills/` for PR review, advisory review and remediation, vulnerability impact assessment, and release notes. Document discovery, prerequisites (including `jq` and ripgrep), and invocation, and link them from contributor and agent guidance so AI-assisted maintenance uses shared, reviewable instructions. Verify returning contributors with a server-filtered search for PRs merged at or before the base release cutoff, rather than a limited recent-history sample. Remove local-author metadata and verify the skills contain no personal details or machine-specific paths or configuration. Repository submission rules, advisory confidentiality, and action authorization remain authoritative. No runtime, public API, package dependency, or type compatibility changes. ([#11361](https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/11361))
